From: Realme X2 Pro Linux port <hmhmdcy@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] kcms/mobile: fix Wi-Fi radio feedback loop in the mobile Wi-Fi KCM
References: https://invent.kde.org/plasma/plasma-nm/-/merge_requests/695

The mobile Wi-Fi KCM wrote the NetworkManager radio state from
`onCheckedChanged`. That signal also fires when `checked` changes
programmatically, for example when `EnabledConnections` follows a
NetworkManager or rfkill update. The explicit
`checked = Qt.binding(...)` inside the same handler then made the
switch and the radio-control write race each other, producing a
`radio-control wireless-enabled:on/off` feedback loop and leaving
phy0 soft-blocked.

Handle only user-initiated toggles with `onToggled`, as the desktop
Network Management applet already does, and keep `checked`
declaratively bound to the current NetworkManager state. The
`FormSwitchDelegate` implementation already propagates the user
toggle; no manual rebinding is required.

This is intentionally a desktop/UI-layer fix. It does not add a
board-specific Wi-Fi workaround or change NetworkManager,
wpa_supplicant, ath10k, or rfkill policy. Upstream MR !695 changes
only the signal name; this local patch also drops the manual
`Qt.binding()` reassignment, which produced a transient
false/true/false switch sequence in the on-device harness.

diff --git a/kcms/kcm_wifi_mobile/ui/main.qml b/kcms/kcm_wifi_mobile/ui/main.qml
index 18b7de8..4a7c6f4 100644
--- a/kcms/kcm_wifi_mobile/ui/main.qml
+++ b/kcms/kcm_wifi_mobile/ui/main.qml
@@ -86,10 +86,7 @@
                 id: wifiSwitch
                 text: i18n("Wi-Fi")
                 checked: enabledConnections.wirelessEnabled
-                onCheckedChanged: {
-                    handler.enableWireless(checked);
-                    checked = Qt.binding(() => enabledConnections.wirelessEnabled);
-                }
+                onToggled: handler.enableWireless(checked)
             }
 
             FormCard.FormDelegateSeparator {}
